### Nov 18, 2026 – Baseline Configuration & Vulnerability Assessment

**Accomplished:**
* Established the initial baseline security posture of the target environment prior to active testing.
* Ran a CIS Benchmark compliance scan, recording an initial baseline score of **25%**.
* Captured visual evidence (screenshots) of the unhardened configuration metrics to compare against post-remediation scans.
* Prepared the environment for offensive testing using Kali Linux tools.

**Lessons Learned:**
* **Value of Baselines:** Recording an unhardened score (25%) is critical for demonstrating measurable risk reduction later in the lab lifecycle.
* **Default Configurations:** Out-of-the-box system installations leave significant attack surfaces exposed, highlighting why automated configuration auditing (like CIS Benchmarks) is necessary before deploying assets to production.
* **Documentation Discipline:** Capturing metrics *before* introducing attack traffic ensures data integrity when analyzing which alerts or failures stem from misconfigurations versus active exploitation.
